        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqsuVvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIvYQAEgPC8iB72xqIS8Y5puxty8Y\n/u9/y1HQdP1SVMixn2z3jCCPOlUPNLzHS+fPBFTcxS1tZRDvjOh+UmJhAspGGDOw\nh7ERAWWduDuw3JnpHL7qJ1r1Ae5CQe4z04QavIraOyik9m4cA2flb7Xl+0miw2AD\nnhKQqzsnAD3hIc6+uIxWoGfqebhQPJIN1G7u/hjB46fWmVdFTzn5K9Iy17pacST9\nl3nlr9AVi2dywRmgPTICwJQ9CleStmwl1pbHMgtXnnEr7A5OAy3J2J90r+xilqVZ\nb97hE/0gRrnTAxc/6RiVVUMvfLUljwCCa1B1sBRfmIgwjj2zu/n1PAsto6gh/IJ1\n7u0f4RnzxwDW1J6HnvEBWsusc9CfDDyqvvfJ9u52X9utye8Icxp6fWy81TfUfeCe\nypnkUkZrPimvBeCm9P84XIVk8i3Tu0nnmUJ88aRYyglIGFSd0IwYWvyArotK7F4R\ntAxmCuJBmW2N41tM2Sd1sBTMlA5AfnMZsTiqwqDnJeWoXIsD3bg9qiZzMRYl6Cwg\nYuwLNyBXua+KO9z+M6nk/BYllCG6uEViKuF5gjeqElvuGIzB7H6VQeW8D7cjdVxa\ng4vzBRcZYYBQQuTGcpjrMIaB2U0hypYdNwaXUFK3i3KRS7ya9wO7AbhNqEDIYleo\nj+XTZREXZHrOPJZi/ZcG\n=+i15\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
        "payload": "tree 6799776e634d5ac21e63119e9b3e1ff5f280cd2b\nparent 5760c9244a67c3917cfdcfadc44b710e7f8c62c7\nauthor Christophe Bedard <bedard.christophe@gmail.com> 1790109039 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790109039 +0000\n\nAdd page for the snapshot repository (#7191)\n\nResolves #7188.\n\nThis updates & ports the instructions, context, and explanation from:\n\n1. The ROS wiki page: https://wiki.ros.org/SnapshotRepository\n2. This Discourse post:\n   https://discourse.openrobotics.org/t/announcing-ros-snapshot-repositories/7705\n\nI added more details to this page compared to the original ROS wiki\npage: I found that switching to an older snapshot (with older versions)\nwouldn't actually downgrade already-installed packages unless\n`Pin-Priority: 1001` is set for the snapshot repository.\n\nMuch like the original ROS wiki page, this sort of assumes you've\nalready installed ROS. For instance, it assumes you've already installed\nrosdep. I'm not sure it's worth complicating it more to support fresh\ninstalls.\n\nThis can be backported to all active distros.\n\n---\n\nI used Claude Opus 5 to make the initial draft, which I then\nconsiderably reworked and validated manually.\n\nSigned-off-by: Christophe Bedard <bedard.christophe@gmail.com>",
